    "Prioritize back volume next period — aim to bring it to at least 6 sets, matching or approaching your chest set count more closely. Strong lats and rhomboids are a hidden key to a bigger bench press and healthy shoulders.",
    "Continue your current chest progression since the strength index is climbing well, but be intentional about form and recovery. If you are doing flat barbell bench press as your main movement, ensure you are adding load or reps in a controlled way rather than chasing numbers at the expense of technique.",
    "Add at least one extra biceps or rear-delt set per session to help balance the push-dominant nature of your current split. This costs minimal recovery but pays dividends in shoulder joint health over time.",
    "Monitor your back strength index closely next period. If it drops again below 96, treat it as a priority warning and consider temporarily increasing back training frequency or load to bring it back in line with your other lifts."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Chest strength index hit 112 with strong triceps support at 108, putting the user firmly on track for the 100 kg bench press goal, but back regressed to 96 and volume balance is heavily push-dominant — next period should address back volume and balance while maintaining chest momentum."
}
